   "source": [
    "## The Client Brief: Should Istanbul Build a 4th Bosphorus Bridge?\n",
    "\n",
    "The Istanbul Metropolitan Municipality (IBB) has hired your data analytics firm to answer a critical infrastructure question:\n",
    "\n",
    "> **\"Three bridges connect Europe and Asia across the Bosphorus. Traffic is strangling the city. Is a 4th bridge needed — and if so, where should it go?\"**\n",
    "\n",
    "Your firm has one week of sensor data — over **75,000 traffic measurements** from October 2024 — covering hundreds of sensors across the city. Your task: build the evidence base for a data-driven recommendation.\n",
    "\n",
    "**The Four Questions You Must Answer:**\n",
    "1. **How bad is it?** — What does the congestion landscape look like across Istanbul?\n",
    "2. **Where is the pain?** — Which corridors and time periods suffer the most?\n",
    "3. **Which bridge fails first?** — Do the three existing bridges perform equally, or is one the bottleneck?\n",
    "4. **Where should a 4th bridge go?** — Is there a coverage gap between the existing crossings?\n",
    "\n",
    "> **The Three Existing Bosphorus Bridges:**\n",
    "> - **15 July Martyrs Bridge** (1973) — the original, connecting Ortaköy to Beylerbeyi\n",
    "> - **Fatih Sultan Mehmet Bridge** (1988) — the \"second bridge,\" ~5 km north\n",
    "> - **Yavuz Sultan Selim Bridge** (2016) — the newest, near the Black Sea entrance"
   ]
  },
